Subject: [PATCH] Permit opt-in WhatsApp recall actions in the keyboard flow

Apply after 0001-0005. Live Samsung policy blocks both WhatsApp packages from
recall actions even though screen capture and text replies are permitted.
The context-actions opt-in permits only those two packages. Original policy
remains the fallback; Samsung intent/safety/language gates are untouched.
This touches a different method from patches 0001-0004 in SmartReplyResolver;
no register count or existing label/control flow changes.

--- a/smali_classes15/com/samsung/android/smartsuggestions/service/smartreply/SmartReplyResolver.smali
+++ b/smali_classes15/com/samsung/android/smartsuggestions/service/smartreply/SmartReplyResolver.smali
@@ -3877 +3877,11 @@
+    invoke-static {p1, p2}, Lio/mesalabs/rezoss/ai/NativeContextActions;->allowRecall(Landroid/content/Context;Ljava/lang/String;)Z
+
+    move-result v0
+
+    if-eqz v0, :rezoss_original_recall_package_policy
+
+    return v0
+
+    :rezoss_original_recall_package_policy
+
     sget-object p0, Lcom/samsung/android/smartsuggestions/service/smartreply/SmartReplyResolver;->recallActionAllowedList:Ljava/util/concurrent/atomic/AtomicReference;
